The page follows the shape of the edition's other System Settings pages (sparky-stereo-memory-kcm) and of KDE's KCMUtils modules.
It uses PipeWire (Wim Taymans and the PipeWire contributors) for the list of cameras and the preview, and WirePlumber
(George Kiagiadakis and the WirePlumber contributors) for the session's default video source: the page only sets WirePlumber's
own default.configured.video.source and WirePlumber saves it.
It reads and sets a camera's formats and controls with the kernel's V4L2 interface (the Linux media subsystem, linux/videodev2.h).
Kamoso (Aleix Pol, Alex Fiestas and the Kamoso contributors) was read for how a KDE program lists and chooses a camera;
v4l-utils (Hans Verkuil, Gregor Jasny and the v4l-utils contributors) and cameractrls were read for how the controls are listed.
No code is copied from them.

